```lean
Real.fourierIntegral_iteratedFDeriv.{u_1, u_2} {E : Type u_1} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℂ E] {V : Type u_2}
  [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℝ V] [FiniteDimensional ℝ V] [MeasurableSpace V] [BorelSpace V] {f : V → E}
  {N : ℕ∞} (hf : ContDiff ℝ N f) (h'f : ∀ (n : ℕ), ↑n ≤ N → Integrable (iteratedFDeriv ℝ n f) volume) {n : ℕ}
  (hn : ↑n ≤ N) : 𝓕 (iteratedFDeriv ℝ n f) = fun w => fourierPowSMulRight (-innerSL ℝ) (𝓕 f) w n
```
***
The Fourier integral of the `n`-th derivative of a function is obtained by multiplying the
Fourier integral of the original function by `(2πI L w ⬝ )^n`.
